    "source_issues": [
      "Parser merge in p034: the STD-history question ('Do you have any history of sexually transmitted diseases?') has no answer in the raw sheet and was merged with the drug-allergy question; the 'No.' answers drug allergies. Annotated as no drug allergies (f038); the STD question is left unanswered, and p021 describes a treated urinary infection 5 months ago.",
      "Parser merge in p030: three doctor utterances (confidentiality preamble, 'Are you currently sexually active?', 'Are you in a relationship at the moment?') share one answer about the girlfriend. Sexual activity is not stated directly; only the relationship (f051) and avoiding condoms with the girlfriend (f049) are recorded.",
      "Age conflict: the opening scenario says 50 years old; the raw Patient Description and the note HPI say 46. demographics.age uses the opening scenario (50).",
      "Name conflict: the opening scenario says 'Gary Mibshell', the sample closure says 'Mr. Mitchell'. The opening-scenario name is the reference.",
      "Gold rank 1 cites 'Early awakening', but the script describes awakenings during the night from nightmares (p004), not early-morning waking.",
      "Alcohol: script p025 says two or three beers a month; the note says two beers per month.",
      "The note says 'unprotected sex with multiple female partners'; the script does not give the partners' sex or their number in the past 6 months (p033).",
      "The note PMH says 'urethritis (possibly chlamydia)'; the patient remembers only that the diagnosis started with C (p021). Patient facts keep his wording."
    ],
